WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.290
Take a glass slide, and
rule thousands of fine,

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.720
parallel lines across it, packed
incredibly close together.

3
00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.140
The clear gaps between
those lines act as slits,

4
00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.580
every one exactly the same
distance from the next.

5
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.890
Now shine a beam of laser
light straight at it.

6
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.560
You can't lay a ruler
against a light wave.

7
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.430
So how can a slide of fine
lines measure its wavelength?

8
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:29.680
In this mission, you'll see how light
from every slit overlaps and interferes.

9
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.510
Then you'll compare a
grating with just two slits,

10
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.530
and find out why many slits beat two.

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.620
Your mission: find out how a slide ruled
with fine lines can measure the wavelength

12
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:41.400
of light.
